  "kind": "room-keys",
  "about": "A coalition room's keys (#125): its weekly mailbox ids and seal key derive from the coalition's inner exactly as a group's do from its secret (HKDF-SHA-256, RFC 5869, an empty salt and 32 bytes; a week's info is utf8('reconcile/v1/mailbox-week') ‖ 0x00 ‖ the week as 4 big-endian bytes, the seal key's 'reconcile/v1/seal-key'), and a device keeps the room under an entry id from inner under 'reconcile/v1/room-entry'. The coalition secret's own ids and seal key are listed beside them: a device that holds only the coalition secret, as a follower's does (#124), derives those, and they open no room blob. One message, a signed record (the signer's public key, its Ed25519 signature over utf8('reconcile/v1/event') ‖ 0x00 ‖ the event, then the event's JSON), from the signer seed given, is sealed for its week's mailbox with a fixed nonce, framed as every blob is (a 4-byte big-endian length, the record, zeros, 1,024 bytes in all) with the mailbox id's UTF-8 as the AAD. HKDF from Python's hmac and hashlib; Ed25519 and XChaCha20-Poly1305 (HChaCha20 from its raw ChaCha20 block, then its ChaCha20Poly1305) from Python's cryptography package, each checked against RFC 5869, RFC 8032 and draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha-03's vectors. None is @noble. Each key, id, record and blob is its bytes; a mailbox or entry id is the unpadded base64url of its bytes.",
